  <h1>Astra Dependency Packages</h1>

  <p>This page provides download links for system and Python packages required to run Astra examples on supported devices.</p>

  <h2>📦 System Packages (.deb)</h2>
  <p>Use <code>dpkg</code> to install these system dependencies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="./packages/sqlite3_3.38.5-r0_arm64.deb">sqlite3_3.38.5-r0_arm64.deb</a></li>
    <li><a href="./packages/python3-sqlite3_3.10.13-r0_arm64.deb">python3-sqlite3_3.10.13-r0_arm64.deb</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Install with:</h3>
  <pre>
sudo dpkg -i packages/python3-sqlite3_3.10.13-r0_arm64.deb packages/sqlite3_3.38.5-r0_arm64.deb
  </pre>

  <h2>🐍 Python Package (.whl)</h2>
  <p>Use <code>pip</code> to install the Python package for LLaMA C++ integration:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="./packages/llama_cpp_python-0.3.7-cp310-cp310-linux_aarch64.whl">llama_cpp_python-0.3.7-cp310-cp310-linux_aarch64.whl</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Install with:</h3>
  <pre>
pip install https://synaptics-synap.github.io/examples/packages/llama_cpp_python-0.3.7-cp310-cp310-linux_aarch64.whl
  </pre>

  <h2>📝 Using requirements.txt</h2>
  <p>If you're using a <code>requirements.txt</code> file, this Python wheel has been already installed:</p>
  <pre>
llama-cpp-python @ https://synaptics-synap.github.io/examples/packages/llama_cpp_python-0.3.7-cp310-cp310-linux_aarch64.whl
  </pre>

</body>
